{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Autism\n\nCondition hub: autism heterogeneity, partial cognitive and biological accounts, multi-source assessment, and support framed by autistic perspectives.\n\n[[Autism Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-27; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 2190,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Autism heterogeneity and support needs]]**\n*condition* - 8 sources\n\nHeterogeneity in autism and its consequences: individualised support, frequent co-occurrence, and outcomes beyond measured traits.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Social cognition accounts]]**\n*theory* - 8 sources\n\nAccounts that explain autistic social differences through social-cognitive processes, and the criticisms they attracted.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 646,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Double empathy]]**\n*theory* - 7 sources\n\nThe proposal that misunderstanding between autistic and non-autistic people is bidirectional, and the evidence that supports it.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 884,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Masking and camouflaging]]**\n*process* - 7 sources\n\nDeliberate and automatic self-presentation strategies, their reported costs, and their consequences for assessment.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1146,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Autistic burnout]]**\n*condition* - 8 sources\n\nAutistic burnout as defined by autistic adults and early research: exhaustion, loss of function and reduced stimulus tolerance under chronic load, its links to masking, stress and depression, and a young, contested measurement base.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1384,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Predictive processing accounts of autism]]**\n*theory* - 9 sources\n\nBayesian and predictive-coding accounts of autistic perception - weaker priors, aberrant precision, inflexible prediction errors - and the mixed experimental and meta-analytic record that keeps them debated.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 1694,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 274,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Autism in girls and women]]**\n*condition* - 8 sources\n\nWhy autism is recognised less often and later in girls and women: the falling recorded sex ratio, camouflaging, instruments tuned to male presentations, earlier misdiagnoses, and how firm each claim is.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 2028,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Neurodiversity paradigm]]**\n*framework* - 6 sources\n\nThe framework that treats autism as natural variation among minds: its case against deficit-focused research, strong and moderate readings of the social model of disability, its influence on research priorities and outcomes, and the main critiques.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 2314,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 274,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_8",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Monotropism]]**\n*theory* - 4 sources\n\nAn autistic-developed theory that places the allocation of attention at the centre of autism: what it proposes, where it came from, what interviews and one laboratory study show, and how thin the testing still is.",
			"x": 420,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Description",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 810,
			"height": 2318
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Autism genetics and rare variants]]**\n*framework* - 9 sources\n\nCommon and rare variant architecture in autism, what exome sequencing has shown, and why a risk variant is not a diagnosis or a mechanism.",
			"x": 880,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Biology",
			"x": 850,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 292
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Adult autism assessment and differential considerations]]**\n*method* - 5 sources\n\nRecognition, screening limits, comprehensive multi-source assessment and differential scope in adult autism assessment.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Autistic sensory and communication access]]**\n*framework* - 6 sources\n\nAccess as environmental and communicative design, the cost of camouflaging, and the qualitative evidence base behind these recommendations.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 622,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Intervention outcomes and autistic perspectives]]**\n*framework* - 8 sources\n\nWhat intervention research measures, what autistic adults say about outcomes, and how the two relate.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 908,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Autism support and services]]**\n*framework* - 7 sources\n\nHow autism support and services are organised, where medication belongs, and why access and participation are part of the evidence.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 1170,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Co-occurring conditions in autism]]**\n*condition* - 9 sources\n\nThe mental-health, neurological, sleep, gastrointestinal and feeding conditions that often accompany autism: prevalence ranges and what moves them, why they matter for risk, and diagnostic overshadowing in both directions.",
			"x": 1340,
			"y": 1432,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#D9467F"
		},
		{
			"id": "g2",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Assessment and support",
			"x": 1310,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1412
		},
